# Patrimo harness

Before changing product behavior:

1. Read [CONSTRAINTS.md](CONSTRAINTS.md)
2. Read [docs/reference/glossary.md](docs/reference/glossary.md)
3. Read branch handoff: `make branch-status` (or `docs/agent/branches/<slug>/PROGRESS.md`); on `main`, root [PROGRESS.md](PROGRESS.md)
4. Read the colocated `ARCHITECTURE.md` for the package you touch
5. For a feature: `make branch-contract` and fill [CONTRACT](docs/agent/branches/README.md) (scope / verify / exclusions)

## Stop criteria (Definition of Done)

- Layer 1: green `make verify` (lint + typecheck + unit tests) — always.
- Layer 2: targeted tests for the change — when behavior changes.
- Layer 3: green `make e2e` / `make verify-full` — when web UI, API routes, workbook I/O, or settings change.
- Work **one** branch CONTRACT at a time (`make branch-status`).
- Do not invent sheet names, enums, or reserved IDs — use the glossary and `@patrimo/core`.
- Do not treat implementer self-assessment as done — run a [maker/checker](docs/howto/maker-checker.md) pass on non-trivial product work.
- Update `docs/agent/branches/<slug>/PROGRESS.md` at session end. Prefer a run log under `docs/agent/runs/` when the contract is non-trivial.
- On merge: sync root [FEATURES.md](FEATURES.md) matrix if platform status changed.

## Doc placement

Mechanics live next to code (`ARCHITECTURE.md`). Decisions live in `docs/adr/`. See [docs/DOC_MODEL.md](docs/DOC_MODEL.md).
